-- title:
--   Function field under base change along a field homomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $\iota\colon\kappa\to k$ be a homomorphism of fields, let $X$ and $Y$ be integral schemes, and let $c\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, $d\colon Y\to\operatorname{Spec}k$ and $f\colon Y\to X$ be morphisms of schemes such that the square with $f$ and $d$ out of $Y$, $c$ out of $X$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\iota$ out of $\operatorname{Spec}k$ commutes and is cartesian, i.e. $f$ and $d$ exhibit $Y$ as $X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\kappa}\operatorname{Spec}k$. Here $\kappa$ acts on $X$'s function field $\mathcal{O}_{X,\eta_X}$ through `baseToFunctionField c`, the composite of the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ adjunction isomorphism for $\kappa$, the map on global sections induced by $c$, and the germ at the generic point of $X$, and likewise $k$ acts on $Y$'s function field through `baseToFunctionField d`. The assertion is that there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon \mathcal{O}_{X,\eta_X}\to\mathcal{O}_{Y,\eta_Y}$ with the following four properties. First, $\varphi$ is compatible with the constants: $\varphi(\,$`baseToFunctionField c` $a)=$ `baseToFunctionField d` $(\iota(a))$ for all $a\in\kappa$. Second, for every open $U\subseteq X$ with $U$ and $f^{-1}U$ non-empty and every $s\in\Gamma(X,U)$, $\varphi$ sends the germ of $s$ at the generic point of $X$ to the germ at the generic point of $Y$ of the section $f^{*}s\in\Gamma(Y,f^{-1}U)$ obtained by applying $f$ on sections. Third, $\varphi$ preserves linear independence: for any index type and any family $b$ in $\mathcal{O}_{X,\eta_X}$ that is linearly independent over $\kappa$, the family $\varphi\circ b$ is linearly independent over $k$. Fourth, $\mathcal{O}_{Y,\eta_Y}$ is a field of fractions of the $k$-subalgebra generated by the image of $\varphi$: every $z$ there admits $u,v$ in `Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range φ)` with $v\neq 0$ and $zv=u$.
--
--   This is the standard description of the function field of a base change: pull-back of rational functions along the dominant projection $X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\kappa}\operatorname{Spec}k\to X$, together with the linear disjointness of the new constants $k$ from $K(X)$ over $\kappa$ and the statement that $K(Y)$ is generated as a fraction field by $k$ and $\varphi(K(X))$. It is used in the construction of curve models for modular curves, where it supplies the comparison of function fields under extension of the field of constants.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_ringHom_functionField_germ_eq_and_linearIndependent_of_isPullback.lean

